stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(institution provides the sinews of industry and commerce, or, at all) Tj T*
(events, that one great sinew, capital. The inventor with an idea to) Tj T*
(develop, the trader with a business to expand, the pioneer with a) Tj T*
(country to explore, the Government with a scheme to finance, all betake) Tj T*
(themselves eventually to the Stock Exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is the organisation of capital for speculation and investment, even) Tj T*
(as the banks are the organisation of capital for loans. Its members are) Tj T*
(in close touch with all the capitalist investors and speculators in the) Tj T*
(country, and can lay any scheme for which the financial sinews are) Tj T*
(required before them. Moreover, in providing a free market for the) Tj T*
(securities upon which the money is subscribed, the Stock Exchange tempts) Tj T*
(subscriptions, and indeed renders them possible where otherwise they) Tj T*
(might not be. Most people would hesitate to part with their money in) Tj T*
(exchange for even the best securities, did they not feel assured that,) Tj T*
(if necessity arose, they could readily obtain its return by selling the) Tj T*
(security in the free market which the Stock Exchange affords. But for) Tj T*
(the Stock Exchange, even the Government would find a difficulty in) Tj T*
(borrowing; whilst great schemes, national, commercial, and industrial,) Tj T*
(would languish in the lack of a ready flow of capital. Railways could) Tj T*
(not traverse the land nor ships the sea; enterprise would be) Tj T*
(discouraged, and the original and progressive ideas of clever men would) Tj T*
(decay undeveloped. Thus the Stock Exchange is linked closely with the) Tj T*
(prosperity of the world in general and of the nation in particular, and) Tj T*
(it has grown with the development of that prosperity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Some very fair idea of how it has grown is obviously conveyed by a) Tj T*
(statement of the nominal value of the wares in which it deals. It is) Tj T*
(impossible to form an estimate of the whole of the enormous amount, as) Tj T*
(there are dealings in so many securities which are not recognised in the) Tj T*
(Official List of the market. But the nominal value of the securities) Tj T*
(thus quoted at the end of 1912 reached the enormous total of) Tj T*
(г10,990,249,126; this comparing with г8,787,316,406 in 1902, an increase) Tj T*
(of г2,202,932,720, or no less than 25 per cent. In other words, the) Tj T*
(amount of securities officially quoted in the Stock Exchange is) Tj T*
(one-quarter larger than it was a decade ago.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(                               CHAPTER II) Tj T*
(                            THE MARKET-PLACE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The market-place, where the dealing in this mass of securities is) Tj T*
(carried on, is by no means of imposing appearance from the exterior) Tj T*
(point of view. Of all the Stock Exchanges, Bourses, and Bolsas) Tj T*
(throughout the country and the world, the London Stock Exchange makes,) Tj T*
(perhaps, the least exterior show. The tourist often seeks it in vain,) Tj T*
(and thousands of Londoners pass it every day without knowing that behind) Tj T*
(the suites of offices, with their Portland-stone walls relieved by) Tj T*
(granite, is hidden the mighty market-place. Yet, for its purposes, the) Tj T*
(Stock Exchange, or the House, as the members and even the Rules) Tj T*
(affectionately term it, could not be better situated. It is in the very) Tj T*
ET
endstream
