(by reason of the lower roof just in front of us. On the left hand or) Tj T*
(north side of the Bar is the Parlour, and on the right stands the) Tj T*
(Kitchen, names handed down through decades for the two little sets of) Tj T*
(desks on each side of the Bar. Moving forward through the Consol Market,) Tj T*
(and slightly to the left or north-east, one passes through the Colonial) Tj T*
(Stock and Bond Market, and stands upon the threshold of the Grand Trunk) Tj T*
(section. It will be understood that there are no lines or barriers to) Tj T*
(form boundaries of the various markets. When one talks of a Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange market, he has in his mind a mere space in the Stock Exchange) Tj T*
(near some pillar or window; or, much more likely, he has in his mind the) Tj T*
(group of men who occupy it, dealing, or prepared to deal, in certain) Tj T*
(securities. Generally speaking, custom alone forms the barrier between) Tj T*
(the various departments, and the consequence is that when one particular) Tj T*
(market attracts many members by reason of its animation, the dealers in) Tj T*
(the busy part frequently overflow the fancy boundaries and press hard) Tj T*
(upon the neighbouring space. Thus it often happened that the American) Tj T*
(Railroad Market, touching the Home Railway section on one side and the) Tj T*
(Grand Trunk section on another, overlapped the boundaries of each, and) Tj T*
(eventually, because of the inconvenience, the home of American Railroads) Tj T*
(had to be enlarged.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Pursuing the oblique left-handed direction of our walk through the) Tj T*
(House--proceeding, that is, to the north-east--we pass three) Tj T*
(markets--Home Railways on the right, Trunks on the left, and next to) Tj T*
(Trunks, further on, American Railroads. We struggle by Banks and come) Tj T*
(into the cosmopolitan waters of the Foreign Market, where may be heard) Tj T*
(half a dozen different languages all being spoken at the same time. The) Tj T*
(Foreign Market is in shape like a sleeve, and the cuff end of it leads) Tj T*
(out to the main door of the Stock Exchange in Throgmorton Street, so) Tj T*
(that we have traversed, roughly speaking, the north-west quarter of the) Tj T*
(Stock Exchange. Round that door the South African Market or Kaffir) Tj T*
(Circus seethes and squirms. First comes the Rand Mines and East Rand) Tj T*
(division, then the gold shares to the left and the De Beers market to) Tj T*
(the right, leading into the middle of the Gold Fields and Chartered) Tj T*
(group, beyond which again stand the dealers in Rhodesians, each group,) Tj T*
(of course, covering a wide variety of kindred shares. But, getting back) Tj T*
(to the main entrance and deviating with the structure of the House a) Tj T*
(little to the right, we leave the Deep Level section sitting round a) Tj T*
(pillar and press on through the British Columbian lot. This market runs) Tj T*
(along the north-eastern side of the House, and is bounded on the outside) Tj T*
(by the spacious telephone and lavatory accommodation. The British) Tj T*
(Columbian Market abuts on the eastern end of the Stock Exchange--the) Tj T*
(apex of the rough triangle which is its form.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We have thus traversed the Stock Exchange from end to end through its) Tj T*
(northern half, and turning, we proceed to traverse the southern half.) Tj T*
(First comes the West Australian Market, which is bounded on the outside) Tj T*
