(Upon this market-place something approaching three quarters of a million) Tj T*
(sterling has been spent. It does not belong to the members as such; it) Tj T*
(is the property of the proprietors, who, roughly speaking, must be) Tj T*
(members of the Stock Exchange. When at the beginning of the nineteenth) Tj T*
(century it was decided by the members of the Stock Exchange of that day) Tj T*
(to erect a new building, some of the more enterprising of them) Tj T*
(subscribed г20,000, and they laid the foundation-stone of the present) Tj T*
(edifice, which has been vastly extended since and is still growing. The) Tj T*
(share capital is now г260,000 and the debenture capital г500,000. All) Tj T*
(new members are now required to hold one or more shares, and only) Tj T*
(members are allowed to hold the shares except in the case of these few) Tj T*
(proprietors who acquired them before the end of the year 1875, when a) Tj T*
(new deed of settlement came into force. These proprietors, their) Tj T*
(executors and legatees, may hold the shares although they are not) Tj T*
(members, but in other cases where the shares fall into the hands of) Tj T*
(those who are not members, or where they are in the hands of one who) Tj T*
(ceases to be a member, they must be transferred to a member within) Tj T*
(twelve months. Anyone, whether a member or not, may hold the debentures,) Tj T*
(which are secured by a floating charge on the whole property, although) Tj T*
(they carry no mortgage rights.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The proprietors of the Stock Exchange draw a great part of their) Tj T*
(revenue, of course, from the entrance fees and subscriptions of the) Tj T*
(members, who pay a rent, as it were, for their stands in the) Tj T*
(market-place; and a considerable portion of the revenue comes from the) Tj T*
(rent of the brokers' offices which form part of the building. The) Tj T*
(interests of the proprietors are controlled by directors, who are called) Tj T*
