(In the preceding chapters the Stock Exchange has been considered as an) Tj T*
(institution complete in itself, rather than as an important element in) Tj T*
(the world's business. We have obtained some idea of its constitution as) Tj T*
(it affects its proprietors and members rather than as it affects the) Tj T*
(outside public. The market-place and its frequenters are there, but we) Tj T*
(have not yet seen them at work, as we shall now proceed to do.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The members of the Stock Exchange are divided into two sections: the) Tj T*
(jobbers who are ever ready to buy from or sell to the public the wares) Tj T*
(in which they deal, and the brokers ever ready to act as agents for the) Tj T*
(public in their transactions with these jobbers. These brokers and) Tj T*
(jobbers--there are twice as many jobbers as brokers--are equal in all) Tj T*
(respects as members of the Stock Exchange; they pay the same fees and) Tj T*
(subscriptions, and they are governed by the same code of rules,) Tj T*
(although, of course, some of these rules are specially applicable to the) Tj T*
(one class and some to the other. At the outset a member of the Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange has to declare whether he proposes to act as a broker or a) Tj T*
(jobber. He may not act as both, or what would practically amount to the) Tj T*
(same thing, no partnership may exist between a broker and a jobber.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The system, the advantages of which are often called in question, is) Tj T*
(peculiar to the London Stock Exchange. It does not exist in New York, or) Tj T*
(in Paris, or in the other principal business centres of the world. It is) Tj T*
(obvious, however, that it acts as something of a check in the interest) Tj T*
(of the public unversed in the methods of the market. Were an outside) Tj T*
(buyer or seller to deal direct with a market professional, he would be) Tj T*
(entirely at his mercy, whereas by employing another market professional) Tj T*
(to deal for him he brings into play the principle of diamond cut) Tj T*
(diamond. It is quite easy to bid on one's own behalf in an auction room,) Tj T*
(but it is usually found more profitable to pay a commission to someone) Tj T*
(who knows the ropes; and the intricacies of auction buying are not to be) Tj T*
(compared with those of transactions in stocks and shares. That, of) Tj T*
(course, is not the only advantage of employing a broker as agent to deal) Tj T*
(with a jobber who is a merchant. The wares of the Stock Exchange are) Tj T*
(numerous and varied; more than four thousand separate securities are) Tj T*
(quoted in the Official Price List of the market, and the number of) Tj T*
(stocks and shares dealt in which are not quoted in this list is legion.) Tj T*
(One might wander about the Stock Exchange all day, and frequent hundreds) Tj T*
(of brokers' offices which surround it, without being able to find a) Tj T*
(seller of the certain stock one wants to buy, or a buyer of the certain) Tj T*
(stock one wants to sell. In the existence of the jobbers there is) Tj T*
(organisation. They stand in their own markets waiting either to buy or) Tj T*
(sell the few special securities in which they are always prepared to) Tj T*
(deal. In cases where there is intimate connection between a company and) Tj T*
(a jobber whom it employs to retail its securities, that jobber is called) Tj T*
("the shop" in such securities. Jobbers are often called dealers; the) Tj T*
(broker, of course, deals in a sense, and so does the outside investor or) Tj T*
(speculator, but the term dealer is frequently used, to the confusion of) Tj T*
(the uninitiated, in the limited sense of being synonymous with the term) Tj T*
(jobber.) Tj T*
