(able to keep his finger on the pulse of the market, and to gauge) Tj T*
(accurately at any moment its supply and demand. He must do this in his) Tj T*
(own interest, for he must ever be ready to buy and sell at the demand of) Tj T*
(the broker whom the public sends to him. This is compulsory under the) Tj T*
(law of competition, for, of course although the jobber confines his) Tj T*
(attention to comparatively few stocks, he has no monopoly; there are) Tj T*
