(than that at which he has bought it or thinks he can buy it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Thus he is to all intents and purposes a merchant, while the broker is) Tj T*
(an agent and an agent only, the agent of the outside public. The) Tj T*
(outsider buys from or sells to the jobber through the medium of the) Tj T*
(broker. The broker, except in special cases, may not do business direct) Tj T*
(with his client, although the rule is sometimes honoured in the breach;) Tj T*
(it is the custom of many a broker to inform the client of the name of) Tj T*
(the jobber from whom he has bought the stock, and it is within the right) Tj T*
(of the client even to examine the jobber's book to see that the) Tj T*
(transaction has been properly carried through. There are, however,) Tj T*
(special circumstances in which it is to the interest of both broker and) Tj T*
(client that they should deal with each other direct. For instance, if a) Tj T*
(broker, as not infrequently happens in the case of an active security,) Tj T*
(simultaneously receives an order to sell certain stock for one client) Tj T*
(and to buy it for another, it would obviously mean delay and expense, to) Tj T*
(the detriment of both clients, if the broker had to go into the market) Tj T*
(to sell the stock and to go into the market again to buy it. It is) Tj T*
(better for all concerned that the business should be carried out as a) Tj T*
(cross-transaction, even if in the process the broker receives a) Tj T*
(commission from both clients, as he would if he went into the market. He) Tj T*
(is allowed to arrange the cross-transaction, with the important) Tj T*
(provisions that he must distinctly inform the clients of the) Tj T*
(circumstances of the case and that he must not take commission from both) Tj T*
(parties.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The distinction between jobber and broker was for years a source of) Tj T*
(discussion often acrimonious in the Stock Exchange, and the) Tj T*
(long-suffering Committee was frequently called upon to decide delicate) Tj T*
(points arising out of the matter. The jobbers charged the brokers with) Tj T*
(acting as jobbers, and thus competing with them in their business. You) Tj T*
(have bought your mining shares, they said, not from us, but from a big) Tj T*
(mining house outside the Stock Exchange. The brokers countercharged the) Tj T*
(jobbers with acting as brokers, and thus competing with them in their) Tj T*
(business. You receive orders direct, they said, from certain provincial) Tj T*
(brokers who are not members of the Stock Exchange, whose business ought) Tj T*
(to come to us. But the grounds for these recriminations have now been) Tj T*
(removed by rules more clearly defining and separating the functions of) Tj T*
