(of the market. A stockholder is frequently called a shareholder even by) Tj T*
(the most precise, but, strictly speaking, the terms are not synonymous;) Tj T*
(stocks are not shares. Stock is calculated by quantity and shares by) Tj T*
(number; stock is capital in a lump, while shares are capital divided) Tj T*
(into equal parts; although the unit of stock is usually г100, any) Tj T*
(quantity, such as г218 13_s._ 1_d._ worth, can, in the case of leading) Tj T*
(stocks, be bought, whilst shares, which are usually of the denomination) Tj T*
(of г1, г5, or г10, are indivisible, and can be dealt in only in) Tj T*
(multiples of their nominal value.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
