(possesses importance because the constitution and customs of the Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange are, to all intents and purposes, much the same now as they) Tj T*
(were then--it brought about no important alteration, for on the whole it) Tj T*
(proved to be a vindication of the Stock Exchange as the Royal) Tj T*
(Commissioners found it. Some minor recommendations for reform were) Tj T*
(adopted by the Stock Exchange itself, or have been adopted since the) Tj T*
(report was made; and one or two sweeping recommendations have been) Tj T*
(ignored, with the result that the Stock Exchange is now as it was then,) Tj T*
(and in that sense the report is quite up to date. In fact, the report) Tj T*
(still forms an admirable essay on the constitution of the Stock Exchange) Tj T*
(and the conduct of its business.) Tj T*
