() Tj T*
(Finally the Commission recommended that the Stock Exchange should be) Tj T*
(incorporated! This was quite revolutionary in its boldness, and it was a) Tj T*
(distinct recommendation, not a mere suggestion. The Stock Exchange, the) Tj T*
(Commission thought, should be incorporated by Royal Charter, in order to) Tj T*
(give permanence to the admittedly excellent rules by which the body was) Tj T*
(governed. At any election, the Commissioners held, the Committee might) Tj T*
(be reorganised by the whim of a majority of members, and its existing) Tj T*
(rules, as well as any further reforms that might be wrought, might be) Tj T*
(repealed. The Incorporated Stock Exchange, it proposed, should remain) Tj T*
(governed as it then was, but subject to the provision that no alteration) Tj T*
(in the rules and regulations should become operative until approved by) Tj T*
(the President of the Board of Trade or some other competent public) Tj T*
(authority. At the same time, this outside interference, it was) Tj T*
(recommended, should be exercised with a sparing hand. Any attempt to) Tj T*
(reduce the rules to the limits of the ordinary law of the land would, in) Tj T*
(the opinion of the Commission, be detrimental. The Commission seemed of) Tj T*
(opinion that the Stock Exchange would welcome incorporation, but it) Tj T*
(proposed, apparently as a kind of sop, that if it accepted the) Tj T*
(recommendation it might well be granted a monopoly of stockbroking--in) Tj T*
(other words, it proposed that if the Stock Exchange were incorporated it) Tj T*
(should have the exclusive right of licensing people to act as) Tj T*
(stockbrokers, which, of course, would do away with the outside broker) Tj T*
(altogether. In any case the Commission seemed to deem it very important) Tj T*
(that all stockbrokers should be licensed. They used to be so licensed in) Tj T*
(the City of London by the Corporation, but by degrees the control of the) Tj T*
(Corporation was broken down. In the event of the Stock Exchange refusing) Tj T*
(incorporation, the Commission recommended that some public) Tj T*
(functionary--it seemed fond of public functionaries--should be appointed) Tj T*
(to exercise authority and discretion in granting and withdrawing) Tj T*
(stockbrokers' licences, both to members of the Stock Exchange and to) Tj T*
(others.) Tj T*
