(are made by members, although its tasteful pages are not closed against) Tj T*
(the work of eminent writers and artists outside the House. It is sold in) Tj T*
(the Stock Exchange at Christmas time to provide poor children with) Tj T*
(dinners. A most remarkable volume, or rather, couple of volumes,) Tj T*
(produced entirely by members of the Stock Exchange unassisted, issued) Tj T*
(for the same branch of charity, were entitled "The House on Sport." The) Tj T*
(first contained articles on home sports, all written by members of the) Tj T*
(Stock Exchange, and yet all written by authorities who would be) Tj T*
(acknowledged as such throughout the world. Cricket by Mr. Gregor) Tj T*
(MacGregor, boxing by Mr. B. J. Angle, golf by Mr. Mure Fergusson,) Tj T*
(cycling by Mr. George Lacy Hillier, rowing by Mr. F. I. Pitman and Mr.) Tj T*
(S. D. Muttlebury, sculling by Mr. Guy Nickalls, and so on with no fewer) Tj T*
(than forty branches of sport. Such a volume might have been considered) Tj T*
(sufficient to indicate the sporting proclivities of the Stock Exchange,) Tj T*
(but it was followed a year afterwards by another compiled in the same) Tj T*
(way with the same objects, containing articles on sport abroad--lion,) Tj T*
(elephant, and rhinoceros shooting, big horn hunting in the Canadian) Tj T*
(Rockies, wild sheep hunting on the borders of the Sahara--all the) Tj T*
(articles contributed from personal experience by members of the Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
